  "i": 3,
  "text": "The simplest sound is a tone, like a tuning fork: a steady wave, and how many times a second it repeats, in hertz, is the pitch you hear. Its samples come from the cosine. For one thousand hertz, the angle steps three hundred sixty times one thousand over eight thousand. That's forty-five degrees each sample, so after eight samples the pattern starts over.",
